          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Generally, a
            %em Poincaré duality dg-algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            with structure mimicking
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
          %p
            On the other hand a
            %em
              Poincaré duality
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            which represents a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            for which there is a sensible notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"}> operator K-theory
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-homology"}> K-homology
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ForGradedCommutativeAlgebras For graded-commutative algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The structure of a Poincaré duality algebra in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              on a graded-commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \colon A_n \to k
              to the ground field such that all the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+forms"} bilinear forms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A_k \otimes A_{n-k} \stackrel{\otimes}{\to} A_n \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to} k
            %p are non-degenerate.
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#LambrechstStanley07"}> Lambrechst-Stanley 07
            )
          %h3#ForCStarAlgebras
            For
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            hence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
            there is the following notion of Poincaré duality, which is really Poincaré with respect not to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"}> operator K-theory
            ).
          %p
            We start with the definition of Poincaré
            = succeed "-duality" do
              %em self
          #PDAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+C%2A-algebra"} separable C*-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              is a
              %strong Poincaré duality algebra
              (or
              = succeed "," do
                %em PD algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
              when regarded as an object of the
              = succeed "-category," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
              its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+algebra"} opposite algebra
            %p
              The element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PDAlgebra"}
              is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+class"} fundamental class
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07, def. 2.1
            , following
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Connes"} Connes, p. 601
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Connes"} Connes
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Explicitly def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PDAlgebra"}
              says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a PD algebra if there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \in KK(A \otimes A^{op}, \mathbb{C})
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^\vee \in KK(\mathbb{C}, A \otimes A^{op})
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta^\vee \otimes_{A^{op}} \Delta = id_A \in KK(A,A)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta^\vee \otimes_A \Delta = id_{A^{op}} \in KK(A^{op}, A^{op})
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              two Poincaré duality algebras, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PDAlgebra\\"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              between them, regarded as a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \colon B \to A
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f! \colon A \to B
              is the one such that postcomposition in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK
              with this corresponds to the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"} Umkehr map
              %span.newWikiWord
                push forward in generalized cohomology
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/push+forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} ?
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          %p
            For more on this see below at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#PropertiesKOrientationAndUmkehrMaps"} Properties – K-Orientation and Umkehr mpas
          #OppositeConvolutionAlgebraAndInverseTwist.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast(\mathcal{G})
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+algebra"} opposite algebra
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivlant
              (since a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite groupoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}^{op}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              which sends a morphism to its
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle"} circle 2-bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon \mathcal{G} \to \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
              the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+groupoid+convolution+algebra"} twisted groupoid convolution algebra
              is such that passing to the opposite corresponds to passing to the inverse twist
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi χ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -\chi
          %p Therefore it makes sense to consider more generally
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
              a
              %em Poincaré dual
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo →
                    %mi KK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in C^\ast Alg \to KK
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          %p
            Below in the
            %a{:href => "#PropertiesForCStarAlgebras"} Proposition-Section
            is discussed how under Poincaré-duality the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twist
            changes.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#for_dgalgebras For dg-Algebras
          %h3#PropertiesForCStarAlgebras
            For
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %h4#PropertiesCAstDualsAndTwists Duals and twists
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec-structure"} spin^c-structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K^\bullet(X) \simeq K_\bullet(X)
                    \\,.
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Connes"}> Connes, chapter 2.7, prop. 5
            ).
          %p
            (…) The relaton between Poincaré duality on algebras of functions and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec-structure"} spin^c-structure
            is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Connes"}> Connes, around p. 603
            ). (…)
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            is the third
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+Stiefel-Whitney+class"} integral Stiefel-Whitney class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mi SO
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_3 \colon B SO \to B^2 U(1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            still exists, but is the same manifold equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twist
            %em shifted
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_3(\tau_X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_X
            denotes the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"}> co
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #CStarAlgebraOf2BundleOnManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definitionnotation Definition/Notation
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"}> compact
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
